{
  "$comment": [
    "Minecraft Java Edition versions this app can target, with where each number came from.",
    "",
    "Generated and maintained by the `mc-versions` skill (.claude/skills/mc-versions).",
    "`node scripts/gen-mc-versions.mjs` turns this into the table in src/shared/mc_versions.ts;",
    "editing that table by hand is fine right up until someone regenerates it.",
    "",
    "`dataVersion` is the integer a Sponge schematic carries in its DataVersion tag. A wrong one",
    "produces a file that looks correct and misbehaves in game, which is why every entry records",
    "its sources: a number with no provenance is indistinguishable from an invented one.",
    "",
    "`verified` means two INDEPENDENT sources were found to agree. minecraft.wiki and its Fandom",
    "mirror are one source, not two -- the mirror is a fork of the same content.",
    "",
    "`era` is decided by the Flattening: 1.13 and later store flattened namespace:id[state] block",
    "strings and can be written as Sponge; everything before stores numeric ID:DATA and can only be",
    "written as MCEdit. 1.8.x predates the DataVersion tag entirely (it began in snapshot 15w32a),",
    "so `dataVersion: null` there is the fact rather than a gap."
  ],
